-## 6. CI incident and root-cause fix (2026-09-10, PR #472)
-
-**Symptom.** The first push of this series was red on both CI jobs:
-`Test Suite` failed at the "Run tests" step with exit code 101 and the
-`Clippy` job with exit code 101.
-
-**Root cause.** `cargo test` runs under `RUSTFLAGS: -D warnings` in the CI
-test job, and clippy runs with `-- -D warnings`. The in-file unit test
-`displacement_variants_preserve_expression_information` constructs
-`Displacement::SymbolAddend`, which upstream marked
-`#[cfg_attr(not(feature = "gcc_assembler"), expect(dead_code))]`. On the
-`lib test` target the variant is therefore live, the `dead_code`
-expectation is unfulfilled, and `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` is
-promoted to a hard error under `-D warnings`:
-
-```
-error: this lint expectation is unfulfilled
-  --> src/backend/x86/assembler/parser.rs:324:55
-error: could not compile `lccc` (lib test) due to 1 previous error
-```
-
-`ci_local.sh --fast` did not catch it: the local `cargo test` invocation
-compiles the same target without `-D warnings`, where the condition is
-only a warning, and the clippy gate is on the `--fast` skip list.
-
-**Fix.** The expectation is scoped to the shipped build —
-`#[cfg_attr(all(not(feature = "gcc_assembler"), not(test)), expect(dead_code))]` —
-preserving the invariant it documents (the variant stays dead in default
-non-test builds) while letting the tests exercise it. Verified by clean
-`CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` builds of `--lib` and `--tests` under
-`RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings"` and by both CI jobs going green.
-
-**Lesson recorded.** Any in-file test that *constructs* a type carrying a
-dead-code expectation must either scope the expectation with `not(test)`
-or make the production code genuinely live. The local CI mirror now runs
-the `cargo-test` gate with the same `-D warnings` flags as CI
-(`build_lccc_fast.sh` publishes the resolved RUSTFLAGS to
-`target/lccc-rustflags`, which the `cargo_test_repeated` gate applies), so
-this class of failure is caught by `ci_local.sh` before it can reach the
-PR.
-
-**Rebase.** The series has been rebased onto `origin/main` 38342a5
-(PR #473, APX assembler work) from the original base 919572c.
