-## 9. Addendum (2026-09-07): second CI incident — PR #432, regression-corpus APIC-ID flake
-
-**Symptom:** PR #432 (the v2 patch as a fresh PR) failed the same Test
-Suite job one step earlier: “Run regression corpus with SSA validation”.
-The fuzz smoke fixed in §8 never even ran. The annotation showed a
-genuine differential mismatch:
-
-    lccc: OK eax=00a10f11 ebx=00100800 ecx=feda3203 edx=178bfbff
-    gcc : OK eax=00a10f11 ebx=02100800 ecx=feda3203 edx=178bfbff
-
-**Root cause:** CPUID leaf-1 EBX bits 24–31 are the *Initial APIC ID* —
-the identity of the core the process was scheduled on. The corpus
-compares stdout of the LCCC-built binary against the GCC-built binary,
-and on a multi-core runner the two processes can land on cores with
-different APIC IDs (here 0 vs 2 → bit 25). The test
-(`asm_cpuid_inline_outputs.c`, pre-existing on main from efa4f82c, not
-from this patch) masked only EBX bit 24 — APIC-ID bit 0 — so PR #431
-passed this step by scheduling luck and #432 failed by it. The old
-“TSC-deadline bit (24)” comment was a misdiagnosis: that feature bit
-lives in ECX and never toggles; what toggled was the APIC ID in EBX.
-A 2-CPU development sandbox (APIC IDs 0/1) can never reproduce this —
-the single masked bit always sufficed locally.
-
-**Fix (commit `e7feb830`):** mask the entire APIC ID field
-(`b & 0x00FFFFFFu`) in both corpus tests that print leaf-1 EBX
-(`asm_cpuid_inline_outputs.c`, `asm_static_inline_pointer_outputs.c`).
-Bits 0–23 (brand index, CLFLUSH line size, logical-processor count) are
-machine-stable, still prove the inline-asm store-back path, and
-eax/ecx/edx stay compared exactly.
-
-**Corpus-wide flake audit (new, to make “v3” defensible):**
-- *Static:* every variance source grepped across all 689 corpus sources
-  (cpuid, rdtsc, time/clock, rand, pid, `%p`, pthread, /proc, getenv).
-  All hits besides the two fixed tests are monotonicity checks,
-  FAIL-branch-only prints, comments, or constant tokens; the harness
-  compares stdout only, so stderr timing (i686_alu_chains) is safe.
-- *Dynamic:* affinity sweep — every corpus test compiled with gcc *and*
-  lccc, each binary run on CPU0 twice and CPU1 once, all stdouts
-  diffed. After the fix: zero core- or run-dependent outputs. (The one
-  sweep hit, `abs_symbol_value`, is LCCC_NO_COMPARE — its gcc binary is
-  never built or run by the harness; its lccc binary is deterministic.)
-- *Stress:* full corpus with `CCC_VALIDATE_SSA=1` three consecutive
-  runs: 676/0/13 each.
-
-**Closed remaining CI blind spots (steps that had never executed on any
-PR job):** “Run linker fuzz smoke” validated locally with the exact CI
-environment (fuzz_ld: 128 mutants, 0 defects; fuzz_elf_grammar: 64
-iters, no defects; both exit 0); steps 13–17 were already validated in
-§8. The Benchmarks workflow completed **success** on both PR #431 and
-#432. Every step of both PR workflows has now either run green on a PR
-job or been validated locally against this tree.
-
-**Lessons:** (1) A differential test must not print raw
-topology/identity state (APIC ID) — print invariants. (2) A passing
-step proves nothing about determinism: #431’s green corpus was luck.
-(3) Validate every never-executed CI step locally *before* the next PR,
-not after the next red. (4) 2-CPU sandboxes cannot reproduce
-multi-core scheduling variance — audit for it statically and with
-affinity pinning instead.
