+# Journal — September 2026, days 01–05 (W1)
+
+Distilled from 57 per-session documents (deleted after consolidation,
+2026-09-16). The arc: IR-verifier birth → the MachInst typed-lowering
+build-out → the PR #358–#364 Tier-2 red-team cycle → the RA cost-model /
+miscompile-hunting wave. The method (same-window paired A/B, red-team
+before belief) crystallises in this week and is now standing policy in
+[`../agent/RULES.md`](../agent/RULES.md).
+
+Entry tags: `[fix]` live defect · `[goal]` measured win · `[neg]`
+do-not-retry · `[infra]` gate or tool now load-bearing · `[rec]` method /
+handoff · `[audit]` verdict on someone else's work.
+
+---
+
+## 09-01 — ir-verify-zero: 396/1112 → 0 violations
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01-ir-verify-zero-and-first-backend-win.md -->
+
+The 08-31 structural verifier, driven to zero across all six opt levels
+(3354 configs) and made a permanent gate (`CCC_VERIFY_IR=1|abort|strict`).
+The first backend-quality win measured under the clean corpus: the
+`movslq` retirement line (matchlen kernel −35.3 %). Loop_unroll's
+two-block carried-phi fix verified against upstream PF-17's independent
+fix — theirs (`init` incoming for outside uses) is the correct polarity. [fix][infra]
+
+## 09-01b — `range_fold` never fired; the harness is the deliverable
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01b-range-fold-and-measurement-discipline.md -->
+
+`range_check.rs` existed *for* the `x >= lo && x <= hi → (unsigned)(x-lo) <= hi-lo`
+Expat/SQLite idiom and fired on none of it — its cast-peel allow-list
+missed the frontend's bool-widening cast. Fixed; `k_classify`
+**−18.7 %**. Two harness defects had poisoned statistics: the benchmark
+harness itself had never been delivered as a gate, and it *could
+manufacture regressions and wins* by ordering. Discipline recorded (now
+RULES §Benchmarks): paired same-window A/B, negative-control passes,
+kill-switch isolation; never compare ratios across reports. Known
+follow-up created here: block layout emits 3 branches/iter where
+GCC/Clang emit 2 — the seed of 01c/01j. [goal][rec]
+
+## 09-01c — loop-aware block layout: `memchr` −40 % → parity vs GCC
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01c-block-layout-and-loop-inversion.md -->
+
+Two changes: loop-aware layout keeps loop bodies contiguous and
+**machine-level loop inversion** duplicates the condition so hot loops
+fall through instead of jumping back. `memchr` to GCC parity (later
+named "Machine-level loop inversion" in the root backlog's closed
+table). Env-knowledge preserved: a harness wipe returns
+`~/.cargo/bin/rustup` without its exec bit and without the `cargo`/`rustc`
+proxies — `rustup dispatch on argv[0]`; `scripts/lccc-bootstrap.sh`
+`setup_rust` repairs both (symlink proxies), since
+`rustup toolchain install` does **not** recreate them. [goal][infra]
+
+## 09-01d — census-first `narrow_copy_fold`; MachInst gets its first tests
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01d-copy-fold-and-machinst.md -->
+
+Previous copy-fold measured 10 insns across 220 files and was deleted —
+right call for *that* implementation, wrong conclusion about the
+opportunity. Rebuild started from a final-asm census at `-O2` over the
+559-test corpus: `movq` cross-family 7 943 · `movl` cross-family 2 463 ·
+identity `movl %X,%X` 261 — i.e. ~12× the real opportunity. MachInst had
+946 lines and zero tests; the session built the suite's first layers and
+corrected two neighbouring tests (not weakened). Key escape-followup:
+`iv_widen` declines whenever the IV escapes (→ 01e, 01k). [goal][infra]
+
+## 09-01e/f — escaping-IV + vectorized-counter miscompile, fixed properly
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01e-escaping-iv-and-machinst-fuzz.md, FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01f-vectorized-counter-proper-fix.md -->
+
+01e found (via seeded fuzz) the vectorizer counter miscompile: the
+element counter was re-used as the remainder IV. 01f's proper fix: the
+remainder loop gets its own element counter; measured 4.5× on the
+kernel with no regression elsewhere. Also from the fuzz wave: the imul-S8
+finding — **no two-operand 8-bit imul exists**; widen S8→S32 before the
+multiply rather than faking an 8-bit form (MachInst census rule). [fix]
+
+## 09-01g — MachInst execution differential + classifier revert
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01g-machinst-execution-differential.md -->
+
+Third differential layer landed: 4000-insn seeded fuzz → GAS 2.47
+assembly differential → **execution differential** (compile, run, hash
+outputs on both compilers). The byte-classifier chain attempt (`a||b||c`
+to `Select`s) was reverted the same day: without critical-edge
+splitting of the shared increment-block edge it breaks SESE
+if-conversion (worst kernel 0.44×). PF-CLS-1 owns the retry with the
+split first. [infra][neg]
+
+## 09-01h/i — MachInst coverage: measured, then 74.5 % → 85.1 %, then guarded
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01h-machinst-coverage.md, FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01i-machinst-85-percent.md -->
+
+Coverage was unmeasurable — on `false` the instruction silently fell
+back to text emit. `CCC_ISEL_STATS=1` prints the census + ranked
+rejection breakdown. Baseline 53.9 % on the spot sample; 74.5 % full
+corpus. Landed: `GlobalAddr` (13.6 %), narrow stores, `ParamRef`
+963 → 96 rejections (proper no-code subset; the earlier blanket-
+`true` attempt broke four tests and was reverted — the rules: alloca-homed
+params and stack-passed args still reject, and the fallback reads the
+parameter's *incoming* register even when a caller-saved pre-store of a
+different parameter aliased the name). Coverage guard: a regression
+test fails if any class the layer owns drops back out. `Call` (7.8 %,
+largest remaining class) deliberately **not** lowered: the rejection
+boundary *is* the clobber model — `Call` before per-instruction
+clobbers is a miscompile (→ 02c/02e close it properly). [goal][infra]
+
+## 09-01j — a 19 % layout defect, and the attribution method that found it
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01j-block-layout-order-preserving.md -->
+
+Self-rebuttal kept verbatim: two listed "regressions" (arith_loop,
+spectral_norm) were cross-report ratio comparisons — meaningless. The
+same-window kill-switch A/B exposed the real defect on adler32 (−19 %):
+**RPO is a linearization, not a layout** — linearizing by RPO order
+split loop bodies arbitrarily. Fix: order-preserving layout (start from
+the existing order, fix only contiguity). `CCC_NO_BLOCK_RELAYOUT` is the
+kill switch (note: it disables the *whole* pass — historical). Two
+hypotheses had been implemented and measured wrong first — keep the
+pairing rule in RULES §Attribution. [fix][rec]
+
+## 09-01k — `iv_widen` fires on constant scales: sieve −21.6 %
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01k-iv-widen-scaling.md -->
+
+`iv_widen` had tests, ran in the pipeline, and fired on ~none of the
+loops it was written for (probe with a three-line program before
+believing a pass works). Fixed to fire through constant `Shl`/`Mul`
+scales (variable scales deliberately excluded). Same-window A/B with
+`CCC_NO_IV_WIDEN`, every output byte-identical: sieve −21.6 %,
+nbody −3.0 %. The corpus run and the A/B *disagree* on sieve — and both
+are correct: only one of them is an attribution. Say which measurement
+supports which claim. [goal][rec]
+
+## 09-01l — IV closure widening: designed, measured, **reverted**
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-01l-iv-closure-attempt.md -->
+
+Widening only the IV leaves `a[i-1]`, `a[(i&7)+1]`, `a[i*3]`
+narrow-derived; the design admitted the whole derived closure proven
+in-range by interval analysis. It miscompiled `sqlite_varint`
+(`8e8824b0a241168` vs `deedcdd4edc1c0f1`) and revealed two soundness
+bugs worth the knowledge:
+
+1. **`Or` range bound is provably wrong**: `hi | c` is not an upper
+   bound (`x∈[1,2], c=2` yields max 3 vs bound 2). Interval machinery
+   must do bitwise range analysis for `Or` or not admit it.
+2. **Trip bound read from the wrong comparison**: any `Cmp` mentioning
+   the counter is not the exit condition.
+
+Shipped instead: the missing correctness gate —
+`scripts/check_benchmark_outputs.sh` compiles/runs/diffs every
+`tests/benchmark/programs/*.c` at all four opt levels (~4 min, no
+timing); 152/152. **A miscompile had passed all 563 regression tests
+because those kernels were only ever built by the timing harness.**
+Retry needs the seed-relation membership proof (record which closure
+value each member derives from + `debug_assert!`); prize already
+quantified: sieve −26.5 %, tls_seg −5.7 %, loop_patterns −6.5 %. [fix][infra][neg]
+
