+## 09-03 — `o2_vla_fill`: narrow store of a large immediate
+<!-- src: engineering/BUG-2026-09-03-O2-vla-store-miscompile.md, AUDIT-2026-09-03-PR363-and-rebase.md, AUDIT-2026-09-03-PR363-364-direct-stores-and-zero-guards.md -->
+
+Slot-stress extended beyond seeds 1..20 hit seed 32 at -O2/-O3 in all
+four layout configurations (layout-independent = the tell). Root: `Store
+{ val: Const(I64(v)), ty: U32 }` (VLA fill `b[i] = 6u*2654435761u + i`)
+lowered to `Mov { Imm(v), mem, S32 }`, and the emitter's large-immediate
+branch ignored `size` and always used the S64 shape. Contract fixed
+(`b10ef6c0`): the `mov{b,w,l}` immediate field is a RAW {8,16,32}-bit
+value — a direct sized `movl $3041712678, mem` truncates by hardware to
+exactly the destination width; the relay (%rax at operand width) stays
+only for S64-dest >i32. Upstream fixed the same bug independently in
+#363 via the relay: ours is strictly better (8 → 4 insns, 0 %rax
+clobbers; kept theirs where it is the right form). Also deduped
+clz/ctz zero-guards at IR level for every backend, and an isel fix:
+**never split a volatile F64/D64 const store into two movl halves**.
+Evidence: slot-stress 1..45 × 5 levels = 900/900; pins:
+`vla_largeconst_u32_fill.c`, `wide_const_imm_stores.c` +
+`check_wide_const_imm_stores.sh` (default + `CCC_MI_ALL_CLASSIC=1`). [fix]
