+## 09-04 — PR #426 CI root cause; narrow-condition width; peephole-oracle audit
+<!-- src: engineering/PR426-CI-I686-ROOT-CAUSE.md, AUDIT-2026-09-04-narrow-condition-test-width.md, AUDIT-2026-09-04-ultimate-vs-rebase.md, engineering/notes/2026-09-04-peephole-oracle-audit-447ea90e.md, engineering/notes/2026-09-04-phi-coalesce-rebase-5649e27.md -->
+
+PR #426's i686 SIGSEGVs were **environment**: `/lib/ld-linux.so.2`
+present but `/usr/lib32` missing — an incomplete multilib host links a
+dynamically-linked ELF32 whose libc startup image is malformed and
+SIGSEGVs *before* the C function runs. CI now installs `gcc-multilib`
++ `libc6-dev-i386` first; without them the torture runner reports 1676
+`reference-compile-skip` and **passes vacuously** — check the pass
+count, not just exit status (a trap that recurred all month). Agent Z's
+MachInst narrow-slot promotion adopted (sound width argument:
+S64 substitutions can't read a 4-byte spill slot; promote to a window
+register, reload S32 = zero-extend defines full GPR); their
+release-build/reduced-target CI changes rejected. Narrow-condition
+repair (`%cl`/`%cx`/`%ecx` width-matched names on the classic compare
+emitters incl. replay) and the "ultimate" tree A/B adjudicated; PRs
+#396–#400 peephole-oracle audit green (1854 unit); 09-04 rebase note:
+upstream #393 pulled in what had been lost-session work (base split-latch
+phi coalescing, `%rdx` param-homing gate, CVP depth-capped look-through,
+vec_load_sink use-site remap, dead_writes LEA-fold) — taken from
+upstream in conflict resolution; only the surviving own layer
