+## 09-05 — RA cost-model camp + torture: the five-miscompile day
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-05-regalloc-cost-model-and-torture.md, FOLLOWUP-2026-09-05d-ra06-and-key-injectivity.md -->
+
+Four miscompiles fixed in session 5-1 (`iv_widen` float-conversion
+closure — 10 shapes; `builtin_size_t_arg_width`; nested-function static
+chain in regalloc; `DivRem` pair opposite flavour; `vector_guard_sum`
+pre-existing exposed). Session 5-4 found five more, all **silent
+wrong-address / deleted-access** classes — the canonical address-key
+soundness rules landed here:
+
+- A cast in an address key may be descended only when provably
+  value-preserving **and** sign/half-preserving: sext and zext of the
+  same source must not share a key (`d[i]` vs `d[255]` with
+  `i = -1`), covered-arm forwarding must not reach 256 bytes away,
+  `sink_conditional_stores` must never merge stores to different
+  addresses.
+- The SIB-index cast peel `I32 → U32 → I64` must not walk to the I32
+  root and *sign*-extend it — every char/CRC/tolower table lookup hits
+  this shape (`t[(unsigned char)c]` with `c=-1` addressed `t[-1]`).
+- `rewrite_covered_arm_loads` matched `Load{..}` **blind to
+  `volatile`** — C11 5.1.2.3 requires both reads; match must gate.
+
+Torture state: 8380-config runs, **0 run-fail** on both x86-64 and
+i686 (remaining non-pass = host-GCC skips, plus `pr117432` needs the
+C23 one-arg `va_start` we added and GCC 14.2 lacks). Diagnosis recipe
+carried into RULES: `CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=<pass>` bisects to a single
+pass in seconds; `CCC_DUMP_EACH_PASS=1 CCC_DUMP_FUNC=<fn>` shows its IR
+delta; always confirm pre-existingness by rebuilding at base before
+attributing. [fix][infra]
