+## 09-09 — constant-size `__builtin_memcpy` → native `Memcpy`, and what it exposed
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-09-memcpy-lowering-and-fp-soundness.md -->
+
+`read64`-style `T v; __builtin_memcpy(&v,p,8); return v;` lowered to a
+libc call, leaving a store-to-temp+reload in every unaligned hot load.
+Now lowered to `Instruction::Memcpy`; SROA forwards the load.
+**Both latent soundness holes it exposed are the lesson**: (1)
+`fold_ptr_deref_through_stack` folded `movq (%ptr),%rax; movq
+%rax,slot; movsd slot,%xmm` → `movsd (%ptr),%xmm` without bailing on an
+intervening store with no GP dest (`movq $0,(%rsi)`, aliasing at
+runtime) — `fp_liveness_ptr_deref_alias_negative` returned `3 1`, now
+`3 3`; (2) `aggregate_sroa` load-forwarding treated two distinct pointer
+values as non-aliasing (returned 1 vs 3 at -O2/-O3) — the source must
+be a private non-escaping alloca or the target one, otherwise assume
+aliasing. Regression: `memcpy_unaligned_load_fwd.c`. Oracle standing
+after: zstd_count 1.34× → 1.22×. Cross-backend oracle + four
+miscompiles companion doc (root) carried the ARM/RISC-V
+copy-coalescing ports and the restore recipe that became
+`scripts/arena_session_restore.sh` (`one command: swap, toolchain, apt
+deps, exec bits; cargo build --profile fastbuild ≈ 2m30s`). [fix][goal]
